  ROOT CAUSE, and it is a class: `dispatcherctl.sh` had a $PSCMD seam used in ONE function while
  FOUR other call sites read the real process table through a bare `ps` — including
  report_staleness. A seam that does not cover its own subject is a guard excluded from its own
  proof set. PSCMD is now file-scope and all four sites go through it; the staleness fixture pins a
  fixed daemon start time so the verdict comes from the fixture, not the machine's uptime.
  The live OBSERVE file was NOT touched — it is the owner's operating mode, not test scaffolding.
  dispatcher/ has no CI. This local green is the only evidence that will ever exist.

